file=Legal & Compliance/README.md · l&c:Legal & Compliance Department=**4 agents \· all built** — External legal exposure: real law, real regulators, real counterparties. Owns the organisation's outward-facing legal surface.\n · tb=\| Agent \| Role \| Status \| · tb=\|-------\|------\|--------\| · tb=\| **comply** \| Compliance Lead (department leader) — regulatory feed monitoring, obligation register, pre-launch regime readiness \| ✅ Built \· Brandeis persona \| · tb=\| **scribe** \| Contracts — template library, agreement review, redlining, post-signing obligation ledger \| ✅ Built \| · tb=\| **guard** \| IP Protection — trademark clearance, OSS licence review, infringement triage, IP registry \| ✅ Built \| · tb=\| **shield** \| Litigation & Disputes — dispute registry, case assessment memo, response-deadline tracking \| ✅ Built \| · l&c:Legal & Compliance Department=**Department doc:** [DEPARTMENT-WORKFLOW.md](DEPARTMENT-WORKFLOW.md) — built after all 4 agents completed per playbook §10.\n\n · b:with existing departments=This department owns the **external** legal surface. Three incumbents own adjacent **internal** surfaces, and the split is deliberate:\n · tb=\| Concern \| Owned by \| Not owned by \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| Real law, regulators, statutes, counterparties \| **Legal & Compliance** (this dept) \| — \| · tb=\| Internal ruling consistency, precedent, distinguish-or-overrule \| `Governance/precedent` \| this dept \| · tb=\| Internal control design and effectiveness testing (GRC) \| `Cybersecurity/warden` \| this dept \| · tb=\| Constitutional enforcement, fiduciary veto \| `Governance/board` \| this dept \| · b:with existing departments=Handoffs are one-directional outward from L&C; inbound goes through operator via a dept entry point (no unsolicited inbound).\n\n · ga:Genericisation applied=The source catalog entry for this department was wired to one jurisdiction and one venture. Per playbook §0.4b and §0.5, the following were stripped before any build:\n · tb=\| Catalog original \| Built as \| Reason \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| `vyon-fintrac-readiness` \| `regulated-activity-readiness` \| Named a specific venture and a single national regulator. Rebuilt as a generic "does this feature trigger a licensing or registration regime" gate, with jurisdiction and regime as config. \| · tb=\| `pipeda-checklist` \| folded into `obligation-register` (row per regime) \| Single national privacy statute hardcoded; regime becomes a parameter, not a skill. \| · tb=\| `vyon-compliance-matrix` \| `obligation-register` \| Enumerated one country's statutes (PIPEDA, GST/HST, CBCA) in the skill body. \| · tb=\| `vyon-ip-registry` \| `ip-registry` \| One jurisdiction, one venture hardcoded. \| · tb=\| `vyon-dispute-log` \| `dispute-log` \| Same. \| · tb=\| `>$5K` litigation escalation \| `<FILL_IN>` in each agent's config \| A real threshold nobody supplied. Not invented. \| · ga:Genericisation applied=No venture, company, or product name appears in any built artifact in this department.\n\n · sr(:Skills roster (15 total)=**5 marketplace** (all verbatim per §4.8) + **10 custom** across the 4 agents.\n · tb=\| Agent \| Marketplace \| Custom \| · tb=\|---\|---\|---\| · tb=\| comply \| `reg-feed-watcher` \| `reg-monitor-routing` (wrap) \· `obligation-register` \· `regulated-activity-readiness` \| · tb=\| scribe \| `vendor-agreement-review` \| `contract-review-routing` (wrap) \· `contract-library` \· `obligation-extraction` \| · tb=\| guard \| `clearance` \· `oss-review` \· `infringement-triage` \| `ip-routing` (ONE wrapper for all 3) \· `ip-registry` \| · tb=\| shield \| `case-assessment-memo` \| `dispute-log` \| · sr(:Skills roster (15 total)=Marketplace sources:\n- [anthropics/claude-for-legal](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-for-legal) — regulatory-legal, commercial-legal, ip-legal\n- [HHHHHejia/awesome-legal-aiagent-skills](https://github.com/HHHHHejia/awesome-legal-aiagent-skills) — litigation-dispute-resolution\n\n · bs:Build state=All 4 agents fully built: skills \· operational (5 subfolders each) \· logical placeholder (touch 1 complete) \· identity (leader only) \· agent.md. Every agent compiled clean; every `.md` has a `.toon` twin; every skill file chunked in the RAG index; every routing row in the root `CLAUDE.md` §2 rail.\n\n**Fleet count contribution:** +4 agents (from 46 to 50 addressable).\n